  "title": "CHAPTER 7 : SOUND",
  "order": 100,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "s8j75b5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO SOUND"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Sound is produced through vibrations and travels as longitudinal waves through a medium.",
        "Key sound characteristics include pitch, loudness, speed, and frequency range.",
        "Echo and SONAR utilize the reflection of sound waves for detection and distance measurement.",
        "Human hearing is limited to a specific audible range, beyond which sound can lead to noise pollution."
      ],
      "id": "x996qc2"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Chapter",
          "value": "Chapter 7",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
